From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: exynos9830: enable power efficient workqueues

With ECS (and the cpus the energy aware placement leaves idle) a spared
Mongoose core stays power gated in C2 almost all the time, but it still
woke about once per second, mostly for its mct_tick timer: work queued
on per-cpu workqueues runs on the cpu that queued it, so its timers keep
firing there. Make workqueues created with WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT unbound by
default (workqueue.power_efficient=1), as most Android kernels do, so
that work runs on a cpu that is already awake and idle cores are left
alone. Timer migration is already on.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
index 7af82cf..822f853 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/exynos9830_defconfig
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@ CONFIG_PM_SLEEP_DEBUG=y
 # CONFIG_DPM_WATCHDOG is not set
 CONFIG_PM_CLK=y
 CONFIG_PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS=y
-# CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT is not set
+CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT=y
 CONFIG_PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS_SLEEP=y
 CONFIG_PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS_OF=y
 CONFIG_CPU_PM=y
